      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/stevenfiorillo/status/2042577468825980990",
      "text": "🔔 Morning Brief — What You Need to Know Before the Open\n\nMarkets & Futures\n\nS&P +0.6%, NASDAQ +0.8%, DOW +0.5%\nVIX down ~5% to roughly 20 — fear is easing but still elevated\nWednesday's ceasefire rally holding, but follow-through is cautious\n\nMacro Backdrop\n\n10-year yield at ~4.26%, 2-year at 3.78% (48 bps spread)\n~25% probability of a rate cut by year-end now priced in\nFed March minutes: policymakers still open to hikes if inflation exceeds 2%\nOil near $100/barrel throws a wrench into the soft landing narrative\n\nEnergy & Geopolitics\n\nStrait of Hormuz remains effectively closed — only a handful of ships got through since the ceasefire, no oil tankers\nIran charging $1M+ per vessel for passage\nWTI crude up ~1-2% pre-market to roughly $98.50\nPhilippines declared a national energy emergency on March 24 — oil reserves dropped from 57 to 45 days of supply as a country that imports 98% of its oil from the Middle East\nThe $4 billion MTerra Solar project north of Manila — already under construction since late 2024 — has begun exporting 85 MW to the grid. When fully completed, its 3,500 MWp of solar capacity will make it the world's largest integrated solar-plus-storage facility\nSouth Korea sending a special envoy to Tehran for its 26 stranded vessels\n\nAmazon / Jassy Letter\n\n$200 billion in capex committed for 2026\nAWS AI revenue hit a $15 billion annual run rate\nCustom chip business (Graviton, Trainium, Nitro) generating $20B+/year at triple-digit growth\nTrainium 2 largely sold out, Trainium 3 nearly fully subscribed, Trainium 4 being reserved 18 months early\nStock closed up 5.6% on the letter\n\nTubi / Streaming\n\nFirst major streamer to launch a native app inside ChatGPT\n100M+ monthly active users, crossed $1B in annual revenue, turned profitable in 2025\nFree ad-supported model competing for younger viewers' attention with AI-powered discovery instead of premium content\n\nWashington Political Drama\n\nDemocrats pushing War Powers Act vote when Congress reconvenes\n70+ lawmakers have called for Trump's removal via impeachment or 25th Amendment\nNotable crossover: former congresswoman Marjorie Taylor Greene, Tucker Carlson, and Alex Jones joined the calls\n\nWhat to Watch This Weekend\n\nUS-Iran talks begin Saturday in Islamabad led by VP Vance — first direct negotiations since the war began\nIf WTI breaks and holds above $100, the inflation narrative changes completely\nDefense stocks and energy names volatile in both directions\n\nWednesday's ceasefire euphoria was premature. Markets are recalibrating to a conflict that could drag on for months. The Islamabad talks are the next real inflection point.",
